fxpulse was newly written for its owner in November 2026.

Methodological inspiration: the open-source project "day-trader-skill" by
Jake Schincariol (https://github.com/Jakeschincariol/day-trader-skill, MIT
License), whose README publicly describes its session-replay method. No code
from that project is copied into this repository; fxpulse re-implements the
described method for the forex market.

Data used by the tools belongs to its respective providers (Yahoo Finance,
Frankfurter / central banks, GDELT Project, Twelve Data) and is fetched by
each user from the providers' own endpoints under each provider's terms.
